[%out 8451] [%in 2] [%cacheread 0] [%cachewrite 2106] The red cannon on e2 is
stuck. If it leaves the e-file, the black cannon on e3 checks my king through
my advisor on e1. It also has no defender, so the black rook on b2 threatens to
take it. My plan is 马三进五 (g2e3), taking the black cannon on e3: - **What it
gains:** it removes black's most dangerous attacker and lifts the pin, so my
cannon on e2 is free to move. - **What it costs:** my knight leaves g2, which
opens the g-file. Black's rook on g5 can then take my rook on g1, and nothing
defends it. - **Why I still prefer it:** the other options also lose material,
and this one at least keeps my cannon and knight for defense. If black takes
the cannon on e2 instead, I can take the black rook on g5 with my rook. }
