马７进６ 25. 帅六退一 { [%emt 0:00:45] [%think 3261] [%out 3548] [%in 2]
[%cacheread 0] [%cachewrite 2283] Red is far behind in material. The main
danger is to my king: Black threatens 车平4 (c5d5), checking down the d-file. I
also considered 炮五平六 (e2d2) to block the d-file. But once the cannon leaves
e2, Black plays 马6进5 (f5e3) with check. After 帅六退一 (d1d0), 车3进5 (c5c0)
is then mate. So the cannon must stay on e2, where it blocks that knight's
route to d1. Moving the king back to d0 first is steadier: - If Black checks
with 车平4 (c5d5), the king can step to e0. The advisor on e1 and the cannon on
e2 then shield the e-file. - If Black plays 车7平5 (g1e1) to capture the
advisor, 仕四进五 (f0e1) recaptures, and that trade favors Red. } 马６进７ 26.
